  "description": {
    "text": "The Pikachu World Collection was sold only at Pokémon Park 2000, held at the University of Sydney from 12 September to 4 October 2000 alongside the Sydney Olympics. It is a single nine-pocket page of nine Pikachu, each an earlier Pikachu card reprinted in one of nine languages: English, German, French, Dutch, Italian, Portuguese, Spanish, Chinese and Korean. Seven reprint Wizards Black Star Promos (1, 4 and 24 to 28), one Jungle's Pikachu and one Base Set's, each keeping its number, and every card has a gold Pikachu-tail stamp outside the lower-left corner of its picture. All nine are non-holo, so the English Birthday Pikachu lacks the promo's holofoil. The page was published by Wizards of the Coast and distributed in Australia by Nintendo Australia. Ten years later, in 2010, a second Pikachu World Collection held nine new Pikachu cards instead of reprints.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Pikachu World Collection (TCG)",
        "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pikachu_World_Collection_(TCG)"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: the sealed Pikachu World Collection page (photo)",
        "url": "https://archives.bulbagarden.net/media/upload/5/57/Pikachu-World-Collection-binder.jpg"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: Pikachu World Collection _____'s Pikachu (24/Wizards Black Star English Promo)",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/card/pikachu-world-collection-_____s-pikachu-24-wizards-black-star-english-promo/"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
